{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And your ears, etc.</b> The sense is: with your eyes you will see your teacher before you, and likewise behind you you will hear the words of the prophets and the rebukers. Some say this is a metaphor concerning the vision of the heart and its hearing." "<b>When you believe.</b> The alef stands in place of the yod of תאמינו. Many like it. The sense is: if you turn right or left from the straight path, you will hear with your ears your teacher in the good path."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:02.684937801Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}